course: dictionary
lesson: 10894
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one to use. The word virgin is a good example. It can be a noun, as in «the Virgin Mary», or an adjective, as in «virgin snow». Look at the words around it to find the right meaning.
explain: Virgin, used as an adjective, means never used, touched or spoiled. «The explorers reached a virgin rainforest, where no one had ever walked.» The clue is where no one had ever walked, so virgin means untouched by people. Try your meaning in the sentence to check it still makes sense.
explain: Some words belong to a special subject. In church, the Virgin Mary is the mother of Jesus. In science, a virgin forest has never been cut down. In the kitchen, «extra virgin olive oil» is the purest, best kind. The subject you are learning about often shows you which meaning is meant.
fact: Virgin, as an adjective, means never used, touched or spoiled.
fact: «Virgin snow» means snow that nobody has walked on yet.
fact: «Virgin forest» means forest that has never been cut down.
fact: «Extra virgin olive oil» is the purest, best kind, made from the first pressing of olives.
fact: «The Virgin Mary» is the mother of Jesus, in the Christian church and the Muslim faith.
exercise: «Female Komodo dragons in British zoos laid eggs that hatched with no father, a rare virgin birth.» What is a virgin birth here? | Eggs that were sold in a shop | A birth at the zoo on a sunny day | A baby who is very large | *Eggs that hatch without a male
exercise: What does «virgin forest» mean? | A forest where children play | A forest that is very old and very small | A forest with lots of rain | *A forest that has never been cut down
exercise: Which phrase means the purest, best kind of olive oil? | *extra virgin olive oil | olive oil in a bottle | cooking oil | virgin snow
test: «Muslims honour Jesus as a great prophet born of the virgin Mary.» Who is the virgin Mary? | A girl who lives in a castle | *The mother of Jesus | A teacher at a church school | A queen from long ago
test: The skiers were the first to cross the hill, leaving tracks in virgin snow. What does virgin snow mean? | Snow that is melting in the sun | *Snow that nobody has walked on yet | Snow with no footprints or marks on it | Snow that is coloured yellow
exam: The explorers found a virgin rainforest that nobody had ever walked through. What does virgin mean here? | Full of young animals | *Never touched or spoiled by people | Very wet and muddy | Newly planted
